fix(tool-market): the alignment gate names which timeframe is untrended

For NET (2026-11-19, fast ADX 18.2, slow 30.4) judge_setup printed:

  'higher timeframe is not trending (slow 30.4 < 20, fast 18.2)'

30.4 is not below 20. The untrended leg was the DAILY; the weekly was trending
harder than either gate threshold. The branch only had two cases — 'neither' and
'slow < 20' — so any fast-untrended/slow-trended pair fell through into a sentence
that contradicted its own numbers.

That is worse than a wrong number: it is a confident false statement about the
data, and a reader who only reads the verdict line is told to look at the wrong
chart. Now three-way, with the fast/slow values stated so the claim can be checked
against them.

Two tests: one pins that a flat fast leg reports 'lower timeframe is not trending'
and never the 'higher' wording; one keeps the genuine slow-untrended case honest.

35 test files, 561 tests.